Un-serialise the generator weight pull.

songhappy/torchtitan's `rl` branch staggers the TorchStore pull across
generator nodes with a barrier per iteration. Because the barrier group spans
every generator rank, the mesh pays one sequential full-model fetch per
generator node instead of one overall. Measured on Sunspot: 13.0 s per pull at
8 nodes (4 generator nodes) against 1.63 s at 2 nodes (1 generator node) -- a
4x factor that tracks the generator node count exactly.

Upstream (pytorch/torchtitan nightly be9c85fb2) has no loop here at all, so
this moves the fork toward upstream rather than away from it.

Applies to: songhappy/torchtitan @ a55da6b4 (branch `rl`).
Verified with `git apply --check` against that revision.

To check whether a checkout is patched, grep for the loop in CODE, not in the
file as a whole -- an earlier version of this patch quoted the old loop
expression in its explanatory comment, which made a plain `grep` report the
unpatched state on a patched tree:

    grep -n "node_idx" <checkout>/torchtitan/experiments/rl/actors/generator.py
    # patched:   only the self._my_node_idx assignment (~line 941)
    # unpatched: also `for node_idx in range(...)` (~line 1300)

